# OpenSocrates for Claude

This package provides the Claude plugin boundary for OpenSocrates
{{PRODUCT_VERSION}}. It exposes one `/opensocrates` skill backed by
{{METHOD_COUNT}} internal reasoning-system references and a fail-open selector
hook for supported local Claude surfaces. It does not
execute the user's requested task, host a service, add telemetry, or require an
Anthropic API key.

The package was generated from content revision {{CONTENT_REVISION}} with
semantic bundle identity `{{SEMANTIC_HASH}}`. Those values come from the
canonical OpenSocrates bundle at build time; they are not quality or host
compatibility claims.

## Surface support

| Claude surface | OpenSocrates behavior | Validation status |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Claude Code CLI | Automatic `UserPromptSubmit` selection and one `/opensocrates` entry | This package's own launcher dispatch is exercised by the release gate on `darwin-arm64` |
| Claude Code in Desktop | Same Claude Code hook and single-skill contract; mechanism and package contract are implemented | Implemented; no live hook-delivery probe receipt |
| Cowork, local execution | The local hook mechanism is packaged and runs where local command hooks are allowed; `/opensocrates` remains available | Experimental; CLI marketplace visibility and live hook delivery are unvalidated |
| Cowork, remote execution | `/opensocrates` is available; the packaged local runtime may be unavailable, so automatic selection fails open | Experimental; no live probe receipt |
| Claude Chat on web or Desktop | One `/opensocrates` skill only; Anthropic does not run plugin hooks in Chat | Skills-only; the customization ZIP upload path is unvalidated |

Read the status column strictly. The levels are not interchangeable:

- **Implemented** — the integration exists in code and ships in this package.
- **Exercised by the release gate** — the generated package's own launcher is
  executed against the packaged runtime layout on every build for the released
  target. It is not a receipt of live host delivery.
- **Experimental / no live probe receipt** — implemented, but no captured
  receipt shows the host actually delivering the hook.
- **Unvalidated** — no receipt exists for that path.

This package's native runtime is released for Apple-silicon macOS
(`darwin-arm64`) only. It ships only `bin/launch.sh`, and that launcher rejects
macOS Intel, Linux, Windows, and every other target before runtime dispatch.
No PowerShell launcher is included. Binary signing, notarization, clean-machine
installation, other platforms, and live hook delivery on Claude Code Desktop,
Cowork, and Claude Chat are not claimed as validated.

See Anthropic's [hooks reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks) and
[Claude plugin surface guide](https://support.claude.com/en/articles/13837440-use-plugins-in-claude)
for the host-owned behavior behind this matrix.

## Authorized selector lifecycle

The generated package configures `SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, a
Read-only `PostToolUse`, `Stop`, and `SessionEnd`. Only `UserPromptSubmit`
starts a selector. A compact-restored `SessionStart` can re-inject the current
temporary-file reference. A successful `PostToolUse` for `Read` can record a
grounding receipt. `Stop` verifies grounding before cleanup, and `SessionEnd`
removes remaining temporary artifacts.

For each submitted prompt, the runtime starts one non-persistent
`claude --safe-mode -p` process using the user's existing Claude login. The process:

- receives only the current prompt and canonical selection catalog;
- runs under safe mode, which disables user-, project-, and plugin-sourced
  customizations, including the hooks those sources define, together with
  built-in tools, MCP tools, skills, project instructions, and session
  persistence;
- runs in a new owner-only temporary working directory;
- returns a JSON-schema-constrained selection candidate; and
- is supervised by a 30-second OpenSocrates deadline with no application-level
  retry.

### Managed policy is not disabled

Safe mode does not disable managed settings policy. Anthropic's
[CLI reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cli-reference) states that under
`--safe-mode` "managed settings policy still applies, including
policy-configured hooks". Not every hook is disabled inside the selector.

On an organization-managed machine:

- a policy-configured `UserPromptSubmit` hook still runs inside the selector
  process, receives the current prompt on standard input, and can return
  `additionalContext` that influences selection;
- managed plugins, managed skills, managed `CLAUDE.md`, and policy-configured
  MCP servers do not load.

OpenSocrates does not detect or override managed policy. Selection stays
bounded either way: the model's returned instruction text is discarded and only
authored OpenSocrates content is assembled and injected. Operators who cannot
accept managed-hook visibility of the selector prompt should not enable
OpenSocrates selection on those machines.

The candidate chooses IDs only. OpenSocrates discards candidate instruction
text and deterministically assembles the selected authored theory and examples.
Complete content is written to an owner-only Markdown file. Claude hook
surfaces prefer a self-ignored `.opensocrates` area inside the current
workspace so the host can read it without another directory permission; an
owner-only OS temporary directory remains the fail-open fallback. A backup or
sync tool that does not honor `.gitignore` or hidden-directory conventions can
observe this authored artifact while it exists. Claude
receives one hidden `additionalContext` message naming that file, identifying
each selection as `method-id@content-revision`, requiring a complete read before
acting, and requiring the same identifiers in a final grounding audit line.
When the selected methods' authored `Do not use when` and `Stop conditions` fit
the hook context budget, those exact sections are also inlined as immediately
binding rules; they do not replace the complete file read.

The Read-only `PostToolUse` hook accepts a grounding read only when it targets
the exact current-turn file, starts at the first line, succeeds, and returns the
file's terminal marker. It then stores an authenticated owner-only receipt.
At `Stop`, a missing receipt or mismatched final audit line requests one bounded
repair pass. `stop_hook_active` prevents a continuation loop; if a hook or
receipt operation is unavailable, the integration fails open.

The receipt records that a successful `Read` callback for that exact file
returned content reaching the terminal marker. It does not prove that every
artifact byte was delivered; the model does not author the tool response, and
anything able to forge that callback already controls the hook's input.

Non-intervention, an unavailable Claude CLI, authentication failure, timeout,
malformed output, unknown method ID, unavailable local runtime, or artifact
failure all produce literal empty hook output and do not block the user's task.

Raw prompts, transcripts, workspace files, tool values, credentials, selector
reasoning, and raw CLI output are not written to OpenSocrates records, logs,
metrics, diagnostics, or instruction files. This Claude selector does not read
transcripts or workspace files. The complete Read response is checked only in
memory for the terminal marker and is not retained. A grounding receipt contains
only the artifact digest, content revision, selected method IDs, and keyed
authentication/tool-use tags; it contains no prompt, tool output, workspace
path, or artifact path. Temporary instruction files contain authored
OpenSocrates content only; `Stop` removes the active turn and its receipt,
`SessionEnd` removes the session, and `SessionStart` sweeps crash leftovers
older than 24 hours.

## Package contents

- Manifest: `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`
- Hook definition: `hooks/hooks.json`
- Fixed launcher: `bin/launch.sh`; this exact `bin/` placement is required and
  no root-level or PowerShell launcher is shipped
- Native runtime: `runtime/<target>/opensocrates-runtime/`, resolved by
  the launcher relative to the plugin root
- One user-facing controller skill: `skills/opensocrates/SKILL.md`
- Internal routing catalog and method procedures:
  `skills/opensocrates/references/`

Validate a generated package with:

```bash
claude plugin validate . --strict
```

For local development, start Claude Code with:

```bash
claude --plugin-dir .
```

